# HRMS liquid glass

Before a layout, CSS, PWA, nav, attendance, or employee UI edit, read `docs/prompts/HRMS-SYSTEM.md` and the one module file for that screen. The index is `docs/README.md`.

## Future notes

Create a new `.md` note. Do not append a second topic to a file that already exists.

| Kind | Path | File name |
|---|---|---|
| System prompt | `docs/prompts/` | `HRMS-<TOPIC>.md` |
| Module note | `docs/<module>/` | `<TOPIC>.md` |
| Icon | `docs/brand/` | `app-icon.png` only |

Module folders: `auth`, `roles`, `employees`, `attendance`, `shifts`, `leave`, `holidays`, `payroll`, `salary`, `advances`, `devices`, `reports`, `bank`, `users`, `organization`.

Add the new file to the index table in `docs/README.md` in the same change. A new product module gets a new folder, then a row in that index.

## Do not break

- Blade, Bootstrap, jQuery, Select2, Flatpickr. No Vite rewrite. Filters, saves, and lists stay on the page (`docs/prompts/HRMS-LIVE-UI.md`).
- Auth, MFA, `AccessScope`, attendance math, payroll math, Dahua, Hikvision, and ezapi routes.
- Menus follow `docs/roles/NAV-PERMISSIONS.md`. "All employees" means employees that user may already see.
- Mark: `docs/brand/app-icon.png`. Accent follows that red. Status colours stay green, amber, and red.
- Liquid glass is chrome only, with a solid fallback for `prefers-reduced-transparency`.
- PWA caches the app shell only, never employee, payroll, or device payloads.
